      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think this needs to be a bit field. It seems like the only thing that\u0027s being used for is to allow checking for sink connect and disconnect with this line of code in usbc_ppc.c:\nif (dev \u0026 PPC_DEV_SNK)\n\nHowever, I think this can be replaced with something like\nif (dev \u003d\u003d PPC_DEV_SNK) for the connected case and an unconditional clear for the disconnected case. (Clearing the sink-connected bit when a source is disconnected is a no-op.)\n\nWith the semantics I describe, I think a better name for the third enum value would be \"PPC_DEV_DISCONNECTED.\"",
